 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "To find the value of an expression, replace each letter by its number (substitute), then work it out. Multiply and divide before you add and subtract.\n3x + 2 when x = 4: 3 × 4 + 2 = 12 + 2 = 14.\nPut a negative number in brackets: 2a − b when a = 3 and b = −1: 2 × 3 − (−1) = 6 + 1 = 7.\nTwo letters next to each other are multiplied: 5xy when x = 2 and y = 3 is 5 × 2 × 3 = 30.\nPowers come first: x² when x = −3 is (−3)² = 9. And 3x² means 3 × x², so when x = 2 it is 3 × 4 = 12.\nSimplify first when you can: 3x + 2y − x + y = 2x + 3y.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "a": 3,
   "b": -2,
   "c": 5
  },
  "problem": "Find the value of {mono(a, 'x²')} − {c}y when x = {b} and y = {b}.",
  "steps": [
   "Substitute, with brackets for the negative number: {a} × {br(b)}² − {c} × {br(b)}.",
   "Power first: {br(b)}² = {b * b}, so {a} × {b * b} = {a * b * b}.",
   "{c} × {br(b)} = {c * b}.",
   "{a * b * b} − {br(c * b)} = {a * b * b} + {-c * b} = {a * b * b - c * b}."
  ],
  "answer": "The value is {a * b * b - c * b}.",
  "checks": [
   "a * b * b - c * b == 22"
  ]
 },
